---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
import { buttonVariants } from '@/components/ui/button'
import { Card, CardContent, CardHeader } from '@/components/ui/card'
import BlogYouTube from '@/components/blog-media/blog-youtube.astro'
import { withBasePath } from '@/lib/paths'

const pageTitle = 'Bound By Death'
const pageDescription = 'Bound By Death is the game done by Ravenwhisp Studios.'

const lyrielAbilities = [
  {
    name: 'Basic Arrow',
    key: 'RB-key.png',
    keyLabel: 'RB',
    controlNote: 'Aim',
    image: 'lyriel-basic-arrow.gif',
    imageAlt: 'Lýriel firing a basic arrow'
  },
  {
    name: 'Charged Arrow',
    key: 'RT-key.png',
    keyLabel: 'RT',
    controlNote: 'Hold and release',
    image: 'lyriel-charged-arrow.gif',
    imageAlt: 'Lýriel charging and firing an arrow'
  },
  {
    name: 'Arrow Volley',
    key: 'Lt-key.png',
    keyLabel: 'LT',
    controlNote: '',
    image: 'lyriel-arrow-voleey.gif',
    imageAlt: 'Lýriel firing a volley of arrows'
  },
  {
    name: 'Dash',
    key: 'LB-key.png',
    keyLabel: 'LB',
    controlNote: '',
    image: 'lyriel-dash.gif',
    imageAlt: 'Lýriel dashing across the battlefield'
  }
]

const deathAbilities = [
  {
    name: 'Basic Scythe',
    key: 'RB-key.png',
    keyLabel: 'RB',
    controlNote: '',
    image: 'death-basic-scythe.gif',
    imageAlt: 'Death attacking with a basic scythe swing'
  },
  {
    name: 'Circular Scythe',
    key: 'RT-key.png',
    keyLabel: 'RT',
    controlNote: 'Hold and release',
    image: 'death-cyrcular-scythe.gif',
    imageAlt: 'Death performing a circular scythe attack'
  },
  {
    name: 'Taunt',
    key: 'Lt-key.png',
    keyLabel: 'LT',
    controlNote: '',
    image: 'death-taunt.gif',
    imageAlt: 'Death using a taunt to draw nearby enemies'
  },
  {
    name: 'Dash',
    key: 'LB-key.png',
    keyLabel: 'LB',
    controlNote: '',
    image: 'death-dash.gif',
    imageAlt: 'Death dashing through enemies'
  }
]
---

<Layout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <section class='border-b bg-background' aria-labelledby='bound-hero-title'>
    <div
      class='mx-auto grid max-w-7xl grid-cols-1 items-center gap-0 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] md:gap-8 md:py-10 lg:px-8'
    >
      <div class='mx-auto w-full max-w-2xl space-y-5 md:mx-0'>
        <p class='text-primary text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase'>A dark fantasy co-op adventure game</p>
        <h1 class='text-foreground text-4xl font-bold'>
          Bound By Death
        </h1>
        <p class='text-muted-foreground max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed sm:text-xl'>
          In a world where death is not the end, you must face the consequences of the past.
        </p>
        <nav class='flex flex-col gap-3 pt-1 sm:flex-row' aria-label='Explore Bound By Death'>
          <a href='#story' class={buttonVariants({ size: 'lg' })}>Read the story</a>
          <a href='#mechanics' class={buttonVariants({ variant: 'outline', size: 'lg' })}>Explore the mechanics</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
      <div class='mx-auto grid w-full max-w-[18rem] place-items-center md:max-w-[30rem]'>
        <img
          class='h-auto w-full object-contain drop-shadow-lg'
          src={withBasePath('/images/DeathAndLyriel_side-by-side.png')}
          alt='Lyriel and Death together, bound by swirling blue magic'
          width='1920'
          height='1920'
          fetchpriority='high'
          decoding='async'
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id='story' class='scroll-mt-24 pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12 sm:pb-24' aria-labelledby='story-title'>
    <div class='mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8'>
      <div class='max-w-7xl space-y-3'>
        <header class='space-y-2'>
          <h2 id='story-title' class='text-primary text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase'>The Game</h2>
          <p class='text-foreground text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl'>Two Souls, One Destiny</p>
        </header>
        <div class='grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-1 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
          <p>
            Bound By Death is a <strong class='text-foreground'>top-down cooperative hack 'n' slash </strong> built around fast, action-driven combat and tight interaction between the protagonists.
            The players control Lyriel and Death, 20 years after the events of the prologue, in a world where souls can not cross to the other side.
            Descend to the depths of the castle and confront Aelorin, fighting enemies and dealing with puzzles, traps and other challenges along the way.
            Each character has a distinct role, so collaboration will be needed to advance.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you want to learn more about the game, it's characters, enemies, how the world works and more you are in the correct page.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id='mechanics' class='scroll-mt-24 border-y bg-card py-16 sm:py-24' aria-labelledby='mechanics-title'>
    <div class='mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8'>
      <header class='space-y-3'>
        <p class='text-primary text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase'>The heart of the experience</p>
        <h2 id='mechanics-title' class='text-foreground text-3xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-4xl'>
          Gameplay Mechanics &amp; Experience
        </h2>
      </header>

      <section class='space-y-5' aria-labelledby='core-mechanics-title'>
        <h3 id='core-mechanics-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>Core Mechanics</h3>
        <div class='space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
          <p>
            The core mechanic of Bound By Death is <strong class='text-foreground'>the Bound</strong>, a shared system that links both characters and influences how they fight, move, and interact with the world.
            Lýriel and Death are connected by it and cannot move too far apart; if they do, they begin to weaken.
          </p>
          <p>
            The link also grants them a shared ability: <strong class='text-foreground'>the shadow mark</strong>. When either character attacks an enemy, they leave an incomplete spectral mark. If both attack the same enemy, the mark is completed and can be exploited with a strong attack to gather souls for the <strong class='text-foreground'>Death Gauge</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Once the gauge is full, Lýriel and Death can perform <strong class='text-foreground'>Shadow Execution</strong>, a powerful joint attack that damages enemies within the Bound’s radius.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class='space-y-6' aria-labelledby='gameplay-loop-title'>
        <h3 id='gameplay-loop-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>Gameplay Loop</h3>
        <div class='grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2'>
          <Card className='bg-background'>
            <CardContent className='space-y-4 px-6'>
              <h4 class='text-foreground text-xl font-semibold'>Main Loop</h4>
              <div class='text-muted-foreground space-y-4 leading-relaxed'>
                <p>
                  Explore a linear path, facing combat encounters and cooperative challenges. Use quieter moments to regroup, while optional routes offer brief detours before reconnecting to the main path.
                </p>
                <p>
                  In combat, both players complete Shadow Marks on shared enemies, then exploit them with charged attacks to gather souls and fill the Death Gauge. Once full, they can unleash Shadow Execution. Defeat sends both players back to the latest checkpoint.
                </p>
              </div>
            </CardContent>
          </Card>
          <Card className='bg-background'>
            <CardContent className='space-y-4 px-6'>
              <h4 class='text-foreground text-xl font-semibold'>Environmental Cooperation</h4>
              <p class='text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
                Work together to overcome puzzles, traps, and environmental obstacles. These challenges extend cooperation beyond combat and add variety to the journey.
              </p>
            </CardContent>
          </Card>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class='space-y-6' aria-labelledby='characters-abilities-title'>
        <header class='space-y-3'>
          <h3 id='characters-abilities-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>
            Characters &amp; Abilities
          </h3>
          <p class='text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
            Lýriel specializes in ranged combat, while Death excels in melee. Their distinct abilities are designed to complement one another and reward cooperation.
          </p>
        </header>

        <Card className='bg-background'>
          <CardHeader>
            <h4 class='text-foreground text-xl font-semibold'>Lýriel</h4>
            <p class='text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
              Armed with her bow and arrows, Lýriel is agile and can cover great distances or jump across gaps with her dash. She is ideal for ranged attacks.
            </p>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent>
            <div class='prose max-w-none overflow-x-auto'>
              <table class='my-0 w-full min-w-[44rem]'>
                <caption class='sr-only'>Lýriel’s abilities, controller inputs, and descriptions</caption>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th scope='col'>Ability</th>
                    <th scope='col'>Controller</th>
                    <th scope='col'>Description &amp; preview</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {lyrielAbilities.map((ability) => (
                    <tr>
                      <th scope='row' class='whitespace-nowrap'>{ability.name}</th>
                      <td class='whitespace-nowrap'>
                        <span class='inline-flex items-center gap-2'>
                          <img
                            class='h-8 w-auto rounded-none'
                            src={withBasePath(`/images/bound-by-death/${ability.key}`)}
                            alt={`${ability.keyLabel} controller button`}
                            width='78'
                            height='44'
                            loading='lazy'
                            decoding='async'
                          />
                          {ability.controlNote && <span>{ability.controlNote}</span>}
                        </span>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <div class='flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center'>
                          <p class='mb-0 min-w-48 flex-1'>
                            {ability.name === 'Basic Arrow' && 'Shoots an arrow in the aimed direction.'}
                            {ability.name === 'Charged Arrow' &&
                              'Shoots a powerful charged arrow that can pierce enemies at full charge. It has a cooldown.'}
                            {ability.name === 'Arrow Volley' &&
                              'Fires a fan of five arrows in different directions. It has a moderate cooldown.'}
                            {ability.name === 'Dash' &&
                              'Evades attacks and crosses small gaps. Can be performed up to three times in a row before its cooldown.'}
                          </p>
                          <img
                            class='h-auto w-32 shrink-0 rounded-md border border-border object-contain sm:w-36'
                            src={withBasePath(`/images/bound-by-death/${ability.image}`)}
                            alt={ability.imageAlt}
                            width='800'
                            height='450'
                            loading='lazy'
                            decoding='async'
                          />
                        </div>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>

        <Card className='bg-background'>
          <CardHeader>
            <h4 class='text-foreground text-xl font-semibold'>Death</h4>
            <p class='text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
              Death is a heavy but powerful melee fighter. Its spectral scythe makes wide, chainable attacks, and its taunt can draw nearby enemies away from Lýriel.
            </p>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent>
            <div class='prose max-w-none overflow-x-auto'>
              <table class='my-0 w-full min-w-[44rem]'>
                <caption class='sr-only'>Death’s abilities, controller inputs, and descriptions</caption>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th scope='col'>Ability</th>
                    <th scope='col'>Controller</th>
                    <th scope='col'>Description &amp; preview</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  {deathAbilities.map((ability) => (
                    <tr>
                      <th scope='row' class='whitespace-nowrap'>{ability.name}</th>
                      <td class='whitespace-nowrap'>
                        <span class='inline-flex items-center gap-2'>
                          <img
                            class='h-8 w-auto rounded-none'
                            src={withBasePath(`/images/bound-by-death/${ability.key}`)}
                            alt={`${ability.keyLabel} controller button`}
                            width='78'
                            height='44'
                            loading='lazy'
                            decoding='async'
                          />
                          {ability.controlNote && <span>{ability.controlNote}</span>}
                        </span>
                      </td>
                      <td>
                        <div class='flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center'>
                          <p class='mb-0 min-w-48 flex-1'>
                            {ability.name === 'Basic Scythe' &&
                              'Swings the scythe in an arc and can be chained up to three times for combos.'}
                            {ability.name === 'Circular Scythe' &&
                              'Performs a circular scythe attack, usable twice in succession. A fully charged attack deals moderate damage and has a cooldown.'}
                            {ability.name === 'Taunt' &&
                              'A roar that draws enemies within the aimed range for five seconds. It has a moderate cooldown and helps divert attention from Lýriel.'}
                            {ability.name === 'Dash' &&
                              'Moves in the aimed direction and damages enemies touched. Unlike Lýriel’s dash, it cannot be chained and has a cooldown.'}
                          </p>
                          <img
                            class='h-auto w-32 shrink-0 rounded-md border border-border object-contain sm:w-36'
                            src={withBasePath(`/images/bound-by-death/${ability.image}`)}
                            alt={ability.imageAlt}
                            width='800'
                            height='450'
                            loading='lazy'
                            decoding='async'
                          />
                        </div>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
      </section>

      <section class='space-y-5' aria-labelledby='shadow-execution-title'>
        <h3 id='shadow-execution-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>
          Shadow Execution: Shared Ability
        </h3>
        <div class='space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
          <p>
            Both characters must activate this joint ability while the Death Gauge is full. The gauge remains visible at the bottom of the screen and fills by exploiting Shadow Marks.
          </p>
          <p>
            Shadow Execution affects foes around the Bound, the visible line linking the characters, so positioning matters. Enemies at or below 20% health are executed instantly; other enemies lose around 10% health, while major enemies lose around 5%.
          </p>
        </div>
        <Card className='bg-background'>
         <CardHeader>
            <h4 class='text-foreground text-xl font-semibold'>Shadow Execution</h4>
            <p class='text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
             This ability shows the power they have together.
            </p>
          </CardHeader>
          <CardContent className='space-y-5 px-6'>
            <div class='prose max-w-none overflow-x-auto'>
              <table class='my-0 w-full min-w-[44rem]'>
                <caption class='sr-only'>Shadow Execution ability, controller inputs, and effect</caption>
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th scope='col'>Ability</th>
                    <th scope='col'>Controller</th>
                    <th scope='col'>Description &amp; preview</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <th scope='row' class='whitespace-nowrap'>Shadow Execution</th>
                    <td class='whitespace-nowrap'>
                      <span class='inline-flex items-center gap-3'>
                        <img
                          class='h-8 w-8 rounded-none'
                          src={withBasePath('/images/bound-by-death/triangle-key.png')}
                          alt='Triangle controller button'
                          width='64'
                          height='64'
                          loading='lazy'
                          decoding='async'
                        />
                        <span aria-hidden='true'>or</span>
                        <img
                          class='h-8 w-8 rounded-none'
                          src={withBasePath('/images/bound-by-death/y-key.png')}
                          alt='Y controller button'
                          width='64'
                          height='64'
                          loading='lazy'
                          decoding='async'
                        />
                      </span>
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      <p class='mb-0'>
                        Both players activate with a full Death Gauge to damage foes around the Bound. Enemies at or below 20% health are executed; others lose around 10%, and major enemies around 5%.
                      </p>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
            <img
              class='mx-auto h-auto w-full max-w-xl rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted object-contain'
              src={withBasePath('/images/bound-by-death/shadow-bar.png')}
              alt='The Death Gauge shown as a segmented bar'
              width='555'
              height='71'
              loading='lazy'
              decoding='async'
            />
          </CardContent>
        </Card>
      </section>

      <section class='space-y-5' aria-labelledby='targeting-title'>
        <h3 id='targeting-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>Targeting System</h3>
        <div class='grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2'>
          <Card className='bg-background'>
            <CardContent className='space-y-3 px-6'>
              <h4 class='text-foreground text-xl font-semibold'>Death</h4>
              <p class='text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
                Attacks in the direction of movement when no targets are close. Otherwise, auto-aim activates, and the right stick can be used to change targets.
              </p>
            </CardContent>
          </Card>
          <Card className='bg-background'>
            <CardContent className='space-y-3 px-6'>
              <h4 class='text-foreground text-xl font-semibold'>Lýriel</h4>
              <p class='text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
                Manually aims with the right stick when no targets are close; otherwise, auto-aim activates and the stick changes the target. Charged Arrows and Arrow Volley always use manual aim.
              </p>
              <img
                class='h-auto w-full max-w-xs rounded-lg border border-border object-contain'
                src={withBasePath('/images/bound-by-death/lyriel-aim.png')}
                alt='Lýriel aiming an arrow with the directional reticle'
                width='196'
                height='164'
                loading='lazy'
                decoding='async'
              />
            </CardContent>
          </Card>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class='space-y-5' aria-labelledby='healing-title'>
        <h3 id='healing-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>Healing &amp; Recovery</h3>
        <div class='grid items-center gap-5 md:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr]'>
          <img
            class='mx-auto h-auto w-28 object-contain'
            src={withBasePath('/images/bound-by-death/health-orb.png')}
            alt='A health orb dropped by an enemy'
            width='109'
            height='97'
            loading='lazy'
            decoding='async'
          />
          <div class='space-y-3 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
            <p>
              If a character weakens, it faints and gets back up after some time. The other player can shorten this time by standing beside them. If both characters fall, it is game over.
            </p>
            <p>
              Recover health by collecting orbs left by defeated enemies or found inside destructible objects in the scenery.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class='space-y-5' aria-labelledby='shadow-mark-puzzles-title'>
        <h3 id='shadow-mark-puzzles-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>
          The Shadow Mark Beyond Combat
        </h3>
        <div class='grid items-center gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2'>
          <p class='text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
            Shadow Marks can also be applied to certain objects to activate mechanisms and solve puzzles, bringing the characters’ shared ability into environmental challenges.
          </p>
          <div class='flex items-center justify-center'>
            <img
              class='h-auto w-full max-w-lg rounded-lg border border-border object-contain'
              src={withBasePath('/images/bound-by-death/puzzle.png')}
              alt='A castle puzzle area with a mechanism to solve'
              width='949'
              height='559'
              loading='lazy'
              decoding='async'
            />
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class='border-b bg-background py-16 sm:py-24' aria-labelledby='world-lore-title'>
    <div class='mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-12 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8'>
      <header class='space-y-3'>
        <p class='text-primary text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase'>A kingdom lost to its past</p>
        <h2 id='world-lore-title' class='text-foreground text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-4xl'>
          World &amp; Lore
        </h2>
      </header>

       <Card className='border-primary/30 bg-card shadow-lg' aria-labelledby='chronicle-title'>
        <CardHeader className='gap-2 border-b border-border px-6 pb-5 sm:px-8'>
          <p class='text-primary text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase'>The story</p>
          <h2 id='chronicle-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl leading-tight font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>
            A Chronicle of the Binding
          </h2>
          <p class='text-muted-foreground font-serif text-base italic'>The price of defying death</p>
        </CardHeader>
        <CardContent className='space-y-5 px-6 sm:px-8'>
          <p class='text-muted-foreground border-b border-border pb-5 font-serif text-base leading-relaxed italic'>
            In the prosperous Elven Kingdom of Lýndoril, <strong class='text-foreground'>King Aelorin</strong> lived peacefully with his newborn daughter, <strong class='text-foreground'>Lýriel</strong>.
            The child was celebrated as the kingdom’s future heir—until, only weeks after her birth, she fell gravely ill. The healers were unanimous: <strong class='text-foreground'>no magic known to the elves could save her</strong>. Her soul was fading, and there was nothing they could do.
          </p>
          <p class='text-muted-foreground border-b border-border pb-5 font-serif text-base leading-relaxed italic'>
            Aelorin, a king-sorcerer renowned for his calm judgment, isolated himself for months inside his arcane library, poring over forbidden scrolls and attempting rituals he would never have considered in saner times.
            One night, he uncovered an ancestral manuscript describing a forbidden ritual meant to <strong class='text-foreground'>summon and bind Death itself</strong>, using its primordial essence to sustain a failing soul. Aelorin understood exactly what the ritual was designed to do; but in his desperation to save his daughter, he chose to ignore the consequences.
          </p>
          <p class='text-muted-foreground border-b border-border pb-5 font-serif text-base leading-relaxed italic'>
            On a night of violent spiritual storm, Aelorin carried the dying child into a hidden ritual chamber and invoked the spell. Death appeared—an ancient, serene, hooded figure whose presence made the very stones tremble.
          </p>
          <blockquote class='border-l-4 border-primary bg-muted px-4 py-3 font-serif leading-relaxed text-foreground italic'>
            <strong>Death:</strong> “Her fate is sealed. I cannot save her.”
          </blockquote>
          <p class='text-muted-foreground border-b border-border pb-5 font-serif text-base leading-relaxed italic'>
            Driven by terror and love, Aelorin repeated the forbidden incantation. The runes ignited with blinding light as arcane chains erupted from the floor, wrapping around the entity. For the first time, Death lost its balance. A violent eruption of light and shadow followed, as though both worlds collided in a single heartbeat.
          </p>
          <p class='text-muted-foreground font-serif text-base leading-relaxed italic'>
            When the ritual finally subsided, <strong class='text-foreground'>Lýriel was breathing</strong>, and <strong class='text-foreground'>Death had been torn from its throne and imprisoned inside the child</strong>.
            Aelorin had saved his daughter—and, without realizing it, had condemned the world.
          </p>
        </CardContent>
      </Card>

      <section class='space-y-5' aria-labelledby='environment-title'>
        <h3 id='environment-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>Environment</h3>
        <div class='space-y-4 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed'>
          <p>
            The game takes place within the royal castle of Lýndoril, capital of the elven kingdom—the world Lýriel knows, or believed she knew. Its locations draw on dark fantasy and medieval castle architecture, especially in the upper floors.
          </p>
          <p>
            As the heroes descend through the castle, the atmosphere grows darker and clues about the kingdom’s history and the events of the last 20 years emerge.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class='space-y-6' aria-labelledby='main-characters-title'>
        <h3 id='main-characters-title' class='text-foreground text-2xl font-semibold text-balance sm:text-3xl'>Main Characters</h3>
        <div class='grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2'>
          <Card className='h-full bg-card'>
